WEBVTT

NOTE Generated by tools/build-captions.py from
NOTE portfolio-sources/video/build-walkthrough-short/{durations,seg-NN-bounds}.json
NOTE Cue text is the narration script; timings are its measured bounds.

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.583
Most designers are handed a screen to improve.

2
00:00:03.584 --> 00:00:06.403
I get handed the thing underneath it.

3
00:00:06.404 --> 00:00:09.401
Six systems became one platform.

4
00:00:09.402 --> 00:00:12.886
Campaign planning went from two weeks to three hours.

5
00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:16.238
It ends with the part where I got it wrong.

6
00:00:17.144 --> 00:00:19.655
Everything starts with listening.

7
00:00:19.656 --> 00:00:23.214
And listening means being ready to refuse the brief.

8
00:00:23.215 --> 00:00:26.997
At a two-hundred-person company, the ask looked simple.

9
00:00:26.998 --> 00:00:29.711
Build the tools the managers need.

10
00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:31.941
There were no managers.

11
00:00:31.942 --> 00:00:33.450
On purpose.

12
00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:41.108
So every safe, obvious feature — approvals, sign-offs, escalation — had a manager hiding inside it.

13
00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:44.565
The design work wasn't adding those features.

14
00:00:44.566 --> 00:00:50.433
It was refusing them, one at a time, and finding what stands in their place.

15
00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:55.542
Structure is where listening becomes the decision that matters.

16
00:00:55.543 --> 00:01:02.939
At Talon Outdoor — the UK's largest out-of-home agency — the recommendation model was beating the traders.

17
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.474
And they overrode it anyway.

18
00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:10.235
A bare ranked list gives an expert nothing to do with their doubt.

19
00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.564
So the model didn't change.

20
00:01:12.565 --> 00:01:14.803
What it handed over did.

21
00:01:14.804 --> 00:01:22.099
A ranked list of billboards became a full campaign plan — KP Is attached, customisable in one click.

22
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.701
Watch the plan reshape when I switch the priority.

23
00:01:25.702 --> 00:01:27.599
ROI first.

24
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.462
Same engine output — a completely different argument.

25
00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:34.860
One a trader can stake their name on.

26
00:01:35.816 --> 00:01:39.912
Proving means the failure modes ship before the feature does.

27
00:01:39.913 --> 00:01:45.279
On the private-equity screener, analysts are paid to doubt confident numbers.

28
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.928
So no score travels alone.

29
00:01:47.929 --> 00:01:50.542
This drawer is the proof surface.

30
00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.469
Explain this score.

31
00:01:52.470 --> 00:02:00.909
And the number opens into its sources — the board pack, the audited statements, and the one claim that couldn't be verified.

32
00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:05.072
An honest “I'm not sure” instead of a fluent guess.

33
00:02:06.056 --> 00:02:08.773
Now the part that didn't work.

34
00:02:08.774 --> 00:02:13.896
On PTC's accessibility pass, I did what felt thorough.

35
00:02:13.897 --> 00:02:17.915
Every element loaded with ARIA labels.

36
00:02:17.916 --> 00:02:24.521
Then I tested with real visually-impaired users, and watched it fail in front of me.

37
00:02:24.522 --> 00:02:28.307
They skim — by heading and landmark, fast.

38
00:02:28.308 --> 00:02:33.969
My thorough labels were slowing down exactly the people I built them for.

39
00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:41.126
So I switched my monitor off for a week and navigated the whole system by screen reader alone.

40
00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:46.911
The second version worked because the first one had failed where I could see it.

41
00:02:47.956 --> 00:02:51.055
Landing is measured, with baselines.

42
00:02:51.056 --> 00:02:54.303
Campaign planning: two weeks to three hours.

43
00:02:54.304 --> 00:03:00.086
Deal screening: sixty percent faster, measured before and after rollout.

44
00:03:00.087 --> 00:03:03.649
Technical diligence: three weeks to four days.

45
00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.006
Two hundred and fifty people running on one operating system.

46
00:03:08.007 --> 00:03:09.805
Zero managers.

47
00:03:09.806 --> 00:03:15.460
Every one of these is on my homepage with its measurement basis one click deep.

48
00:03:16.352 --> 00:03:17.572
Listen.

49
00:03:17.573 --> 00:03:18.977
Structure.

50
00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:20.120
Prove.

51
00:03:20.121 --> 00:03:21.405
Land.

52
00:03:21.406 --> 00:03:23.084
That's the job.

53
00:03:23.085 --> 00:03:26.310
Six systems became one platform.

54
00:03:26.311 --> 00:03:30.322
I'm looking for one seat where that is the whole job.

55
00:03:30.323 --> 00:03:32.275
Not a phase of it.
